  "findings": [
    "Original SNL42: each M293 inside bracket assembly contains two MX10 studs (3/4 by4-7/8in) and two MX36 studs (3/4 by5-1/2in). Each M297 outside bracket assembly contains four MX9 studs (3/4 by3-5/8in) and two support-foot assemblies. Both bracket assemblies have stated installed quantity two.",
    "Original SNL95: standalone M391 foot assembly and its physical foot each have total quantity two. Each foot assembly contains one1in jam nut. This conflicts with four feet implied by the nested M297 schedule. Do not silently assign four physical feet or duplicate the source total.",
    "Original SNL56: four oil-bearing cap assemblies, two M294 inside and two M298 outside. Each includes one M295 oil-box cover, SH664A quarter-inch elbow, SH664B elbow nut, SH664C Herring No60F sleeve and one3/16 by2-1/2in steel pin. Two ounces of wool waste is a material quantity, not two separately countable fabricated parts.",
    "SNL309(gq) says brackets and caps are issued without their poured babbitt lining. Installed model must represent that lining distinctly from the raw casting and from M296/M299 shaft sleeves. No new source part number should be invented for the poured material.",
